Annual Performance Development Review — Mid-Year Review
Step 2 — Review: Last Six Months and Forward Look
What have been your key achievements and successes over the past six months?

Over the past six months, I have continued to deliver across my core Data Engineering responsibilities while supporting wider departmental and organisational priorities. I have worked collaboratively across Insight & Analytics (IA), FTP/Business Change, Office Services and the wider team, balancing operational platform support with strategic data development, data quality, governance and stakeholder requirements.

My focus has been on ensuring the reliability and continuity of the data platform, delivering trusted and usable data to business teams, progressing the FTP data model, proactively identifying data-quality issues and continuously improving our data engineering practices.

Data Platform Reliability, Monitoring and Optimisation

A key area of responsibility has been the proactive monitoring, maintenance, troubleshooting and optimisation of the Azure data platform.

I have monitored Azure Synapse and ADF pipelines, investigated failures and implemented technical remediation to minimise disruption to downstream reporting and analytics.

For example, infrastructure changes, network changes and Spark runtime upgrades have affected existing Bronze and Silver Registration pipelines and associated ETL notebooks. I investigated the failures, identified the underlying dependencies and updated notebook code and processing logic to operate effectively with the updated platform configuration.

Where appropriate, I have used these incidents as opportunities to improve or optimise existing processing rather than simply restoring previous functionality.

This work has helped maintain the reliability and continuity of business-critical data flows used by downstream reporting and analytical processes.

Insight & Analytics Support and Curated Data

I have continued to provide ongoing Data Engineering support to the Insight & Analytics team, helping ensure that analysts can access reliable, appropriately structured and business-ready data.

This has included:

Developing the Modality curated view and Modality Active curated view.
Providing ongoing technical and data support for the FTP Council Report.
Supporting colleagues in identifying and accessing datasets held within the data platform.
Investigating and resolving data issues affecting downstream reporting.
Supporting data-quality pipelines, ETL processes and notebooks used to monitor data quality across Registration, FTP and Education data sources.

This support has helped bridge the gap between underlying technical data structures and the information required by analysts for reporting and organisational decision-making.

FTP Data Model Design, Build and Remediation

A significant area of delivery during the review period has been my contribution to the new FTP data model.

I supported the initiative from the initial BEAM process and requirements mapping through to implementation of the dimensional model, including the development and review of dimensions and facts.

Following implementation, I actively participated in validation and structural review of the model. Where limitations were identified within aspects of the initial design, I contributed to analysing the underlying issues and have taken ownership of elements of the remediation work.

This has included creating new data objects, addressing structural limitations and optimising elements of the model to improve its suitability for business reporting and future development.

I also supported the business proof-of-concept and first phase of User Acceptance Testing (UAT) by reviewing supporting documentation, contributing to KPI definition and developing curated datasets required for testing.

The first phase of UAT was successfully completed, providing an important milestone towards wider use of the FTP data model.

My current focus is on progressing the remaining remediation and optimisation activities and helping ensure that the model provides a reliable and scalable foundation for FTP reporting and analytics.

Office Services and Door Control Reporting

I have expanded my cross-business contribution through ongoing support to the Office Services team, particularly around the monthly Door Control reporting process and the Power BI dashboards used to support office-attendance monitoring.

I have maintained and updated the reporting solution with the latest available data and investigated dashboard and upstream source-data failures.

Where issues appeared to originate from the underlying data source rather than the reporting layer, I investigated the associated processes within Azure Synapse and proactively engaged Microsoft technical support to support root-cause investigation.

This involved looking across the end-to-end data flow rather than treating the visible Power BI failure in isolation.

I also enhanced the underlying Door Control data by developing a curated dataset incorporating HR employee numbers.

This provides a more consistent identifier for linking office-attendance information with relevant HR records and improves the usability of the dataset for downstream analysis and reporting.

